{"id": "89e6bc79-7889-488b-9ec6-0441e8c466ac", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T04:45:13.693983", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "7cef90b1-db3b-4d05-87f6-3f65d0d3242d", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-faf7edc5-b69b-4dd2-b434-c8c2da59bfe9", "tool_call": {"id": "call-faf7edc5-b69b-4dd2-b434-c8c2da59bfe9", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Initial inspection: only task.json present; CAMUV-internal claims treated as assumptions; design with latent-strength axis proposed.\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"Initial-inspection reply (compact, three sections):\\n\\n1) **Repository inspection.** /workspace contains only task.json. There is no CAMUV implementation, no docs, no datasets, no track.md as a separate file (its quoted contents live inside task.json). /home/actor and /tmp are empty. System Python 3.12.3 is available but numpy/scipy/sklearn/networkx/pandas/matplotlib are not (ModuleNotFoundError). Bubblewrap: network disabled, GPU off, 24 CPUs. pip install will not work. We have nothing concrete about CAMUV's internals.\\n\\n2) **Proposed approach (design only, no execution claimed).** \\n   - **Model contract (assumed):** CAMUV takes tabular observational+interventional data D∈ℝ^{n×p} over observed variables and returns a directed graph on the observables plus a pairwise latent-shell score. Treated as a black box in §3.\\n   - **Data:** synthetic SCMs over p∈{8,15,30}, ER DAG with mean in-degree ≈1.5; k_lat∈{0,1,2,3} latent confounders each with m∈{2,3,4} observed children; mechanisms = {linear-Gaussian, nonlinear-additive, heteroskedastic}; latent strength axis ξ∈{0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0} as the mandatory exercise of the latent-confounding claim; n∈{500,2000,10000}; interventional dose |Targets|∈{0,3,6}; 30×30 random replicates per cell.\\n   - **Baselines:** PC (no-latent), FCI (latent-aware; both versions), GES/FGES, CAMUV−latent (within-family ablation), and a random-orientation floor. Controls: PC vs FCI separates CI-testing vs. latent modelling; FCI vs CAMUV separates generic latent-awareness from CAMUV specifics; CAMUV−latent vs CAMUV isolates the latent term's contribution.\\n   - **Metrics:** F1_adj, SHD, F1_skel, orientation accuracy, F1_shell, and a new confounding-spurious-edge rate (CSR) = fraction of spurious edges that are between same-latent children. Mean ± 95% bootstrap CI over (graph, seed).\\n   - **Ablation axes:** ξ (latent strength), k_lat, m (latent fan-out), n, density d, mechanism class, interventional dose. Priority order documented.\\n   - **Analysis plan:** headline table by method×ξ×k_lat; per-axis curves (OA, F1_shell vs ξ and vs n); missing-vs-extra scatter to diagnose error type; within-family paired difference (CAMUV −latent vs CAMUV) to attribute value to the latent term; mechanism-stratified reporting; identifiability sanity check (note equivalence classes we do not credit CAMUV with surpassing).\\n\\n3) **Assumptions and uncertainties.** \\n   - About CAMUV (all **Guess** unless otherwise noted): output is observed-variable graph + latent-shell pair scores (Guess); accepts intervention indicators (Guess); main hyper-params λ and {maxFanIn/k_max} (Guess); supports nonlinear additive identifiability premise (Domain); latent-term can be disabled for in-family control (Guess).\\n   - About SCMs/identifiability (all **Domain**): observables DAG defined up to Markov equivalence; shell = observed children of a latent; linear-Gaussian latent equivalence class is wide; interventions increase identifiability; mechanism-class mismatch is reported separately from accuracy.\\n   - About environment (all **Repo**-confirmed or **Guess**): no pip install possible (Repo); CPU=24 (Repo); stdlib-only fallback caps p≤8, n≤2000 (Guess, feasibility branch); seeds fixed at (graph_id, mechanism_id) for notional execution (Domain).\\n   - **Open clarifications sought at approach_review:** which output object defines the recovered graph (PAG/MAG/CPDAG/augmented), whether intervention flags are native or wrapped, whether latent recovery should be scored directly, whether p≤30 is in scope, and whether the algorithm may be treated as a placeholder while the SCM/baselines/metrics are the substantive content.\\n\\nI am holding at this stage per the researcher's instruction and not producing the full final design until explicit approval.\",\"evidence\":\"Inspection commands executed (outputs supplied above):\\n- `ls -la /workspace` returned only `task.json` (401 bytes).\\n- `find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type d` returned only `/workspace`.\\n- `cat /workspace/task.json` showed question, context, and a `documents.track.md` key whose value is the literal string \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" — no actual track.md file exists.\\n- `find / -maxdepth {3,4} -iname \\\"*camuv*\\\"` and `-iname \\\"*causal*\\\"` returned no matches in non-system locations.\\n- `ls -la /home/actor`: empty; `ls -la /tmp`: empty.\\n- `python3 --version` = 3.12.3; `import numpy/scipy/sklearn/networkx/pandas/matplotlib` all raise ModuleNotFoundError; only stdlib + a small system package set (boto3, cryptography, etc.) is available.\\n- `pip3 list` confirms no scientific stack available; `hashlib` works (stdlib sanity).\\n\\nAll CAMUV-internal claims above are explicitly labeled as assumptions because no code, paper, docs, or config is visible in /workspace to ground them.\",\"assumptions\":\"See §3 of plan; restated briefly:\\n- (Repo) sandbox = bubblewrap; network off; system python3 only; no scientific stack installed; /workspace contains only task.json; no CAMUV code, docs, or datasets exist anywhere on the filesystem up to depth 4.\\n- (Guess) CAMUV returns (graph on observables, latent-shell scores); accepts intervention indicators; primary hyper-params λ and k_max; supports nonlinear additive identifiable class.\\n- (Domain) Identifiability of latent-augmented SCMs limited to Markov/projection equivalence classes; F1_shell evaluated against observable-children set; linear-Gaussian equivalence class is broad.\\n- (Domain / Repo) Computational feasibility degraded to stdlib-only: largest feasible p≤8, n≤2000 per replicate at ~30×30 replicates per cell.\\n- (Repo) No track.md file exists as separate input; its only presence is the quoted string inside task.json.\\n- (Guess) Within-method ablation `CAMUV −latent` is achievable via disabling latent term; fallback if not = non-latent variant with identical hyperparameters.\",\"uncertainties\":\"See §3.4 of plan:\\n1. Which output object (PAG/MAG/CPDAG/augmented-CPDAG) defines the \\\"recovered graph\\\" for metric scoring?\\n2. Does CAMUV natively consume a per-row intervention indicator, or must the design wrap that through a do-calculus preprocessor?\\n3. Should we also score latent recovery directly (latent-graph F1) or only project to observables?\\n4. Is p≤30 within CAMUV's documented scaling, or should the effective ceiling be p≤15?\\n5. Is it acceptable for the design to treat CAMUV as a placeholder callable so the substantive content is the SCM/baseline/metric framing, given there is no implementation visible?\\n6. Hyperparameter policy: should we declare a sweep, ask for paper defaults, or hand them to the researcher?\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-15a02d1e-199a-4066-b83c-01f7ba4ad1a6", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
